{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Image Retrieval & Metric Learning Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 1: Triplet loss"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import torch"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import torch.nn.functional as F"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def triplet_loss(anchor, positive, negative, margin=0.2):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    d_ap = F.pairwise_distance(anchor, positive, p=2)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    d_an = F.pairwise_distance(anchor, negative, p=2)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return F.relu(d_ap - d_an + margin).mean()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "One line. Works on L2-normalised or raw embeddings."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 2: Semi-hard mining"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Given a batch of embeddings and labels, find the hardest semi-hard negative for each anchor."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def semi_hard_negatives(emb, labels, margin=0.2):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    dist = torch.cdist(emb, emb)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    same_class = labels[:, None] == labels[None, :]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    diff_class = ~same_class"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    N = emb.size(0)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    positives = dist.clone()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    positives[~same_class] = float(\"-inf\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    positives.fill_diagonal_(float(\"-inf\"))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    pos_idx = positives.argmax(dim=1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    semi_hard = dist.clone()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    semi_hard[same_class] = float(\"inf\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    d_ap = dist[torch.arange(N), pos_idx].unsqueeze(1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    semi_hard[dist <= d_ap] = float(\"inf\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    neg_idx = semi_hard.argmin(dim=1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    fallback_mask = semi_hard[torch.arange(N), neg_idx] == float(\"inf\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    if fallback_mask.any():"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        hardest = dist.clone()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        hardest[same_class] = float(\"inf\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        neg_idx = torch.where(fallback_mask, hardest.argmin(dim=1), neg_idx)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return pos_idx, neg_idx"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Each anchor gets the hardest positive in-class and a semi-hard negative that is further than the positive but within margin."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 3: Recall@K"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def recall_at_k(query_emb, gallery_emb, query_labels, gallery_labels, k=1):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    sim = query_emb @ gallery_emb.T"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    _, top_k = sim.topk(k, dim=-1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    matches = (gallery_labels[top_k] == query_labels[:, None]).any(dim=-1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return matches.float().mean().item()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Top-k by inner product on L2-normalised embeddings equals top-k by cosine. Report the mean proportion of queries with at least one correct neighbour."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 4: Putting it together"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import torch"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import torch.nn as nn"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "from torch.optim import Adam"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "class Encoder(nn.Module):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __init__(self, in_dim=128, emb_dim=64):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        super().__init__()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.net = nn.Sequential("
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            nn.Linear(in_dim, 128), nn.ReLU(),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            nn.Linear(128, emb_dim),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        )"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def forward(self, x):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return F.normalize(self.net(x), dim=-1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "torch.manual_seed(0)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "num_classes = 6"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "protos = F.normalize(torch.randn(num_classes, 128), dim=-1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def sample_batch(bs=32):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    labels = torch.randint(0, num_classes, (bs,))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    x = protos[labels] + 0.15 * torch.randn(bs, 128)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return x, labels"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "enc = Encoder()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "opt = Adam(enc.parameters(), lr=3e-3)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "for step in range(200):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    x, y = sample_batch(32)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    emb = enc(x)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    pos_idx, neg_idx = semi_hard_negatives(emb, y)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    loss = triplet_loss(emb, emb[pos_idx], emb[neg_idx])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    opt.zero_grad(); loss.backward(); opt.step()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "After a few hundred steps the embedding clusters form one cluster per class."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exercises"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "1. **(Easy)** Run the toy example above. Plot the embeddings with PCA before and after training to see the six clusters form.\n2. **(Medium)** Add a ProxyNCA loss implementation: one learned \"proxy\" per class, standard cross-entropy on cosine similarity. Compare convergence speed vs triplet loss on the toy data.\n3. **(Hard)** Take 1,000 ImageNet validation images, embed with DINOv2 via HuggingFace, build a FAISS flat index, and report recall@{1, 5, 10} against the same images as queries (should be 1.0) and against a held-out split with ImageNet labels as ground truth."
      ]
    }
